# Navigation and overview surfaces

When you add, rename, or remove **routes**, **nav labels**, or **tool entry points**, update every surface users see — not just the new page.

## Sources of truth

| Surface | File(s) |
|---------|---------|
| **Sidenav** (order, labels, `href`s, children) | [`lib/modules/registry.ts`](lib/modules/registry.ts) — `MODULE_NAV`, `SIDEBAR_SERVICE_GROUPS`, `ModuleId` if new module. Sidebar reads this; do not add parallel link lists in [`components/layout/sidebar.tsx`](components/layout/sidebar.tsx) except icons. |
| **App dashboard** (`/`) | Needs attention inbox — `components/dashboard/needs-attention.tsx`. Not a tool directory. |
| **AWS** | No hub page. Sidebar header is expand-only. Tools from `MODULE_NAV`. |
| **GitHub hub** | `/github` (Actions). Do not add `/github/overview`. |
| **Design system** (`/design-system`) | Short operator-facing summary of tokens and sidebar conventions; linked from Settings. Authoritative class/pattern lists live in [`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc). |

Fly overview links live in `overview-directory.ts`; **labels and `href`s must match** the registry after changes.

## Checklist (routes / nav / modules)

1. **Registry** — Update `MODULE_NAV` (and `SIDEBAR_SERVICE_GROUPS` / `ModuleId` if the module or tier changes).
2. **Fly overview** — Update the Fly helpers in `overview-directory.ts` when Fly links change.
3. **Module-only overview pages** — e.g. [`app/secrets/overview/page.tsx`](app/secrets/overview/page.tsx): if copy or links should reflect new tools, update that page too.
4. **Shell context** — If the path is a new top-level area, extend [`components/layout/shell.tsx`](components/layout/shell.tsx) (`derivePageContext`, `deriveBreadcrumb`) so breadcrumbs and agent context stay correct.
5. **Codebase map** — Per [`codebase-knowledge.mdc`](codebase-knowledge.mdc), note new routes or nav in [`CODEBASE.md`](CODEBASE.md).

```text
❌ Adding a nav item only in a page component
✅ registry.ts + overview-directory.ts (+ module overview page if needed)
```
